# Frame rate: standing still in a busy base, the headset gets its frames. The plugin reports every ten seconds how many
# frames the headset asked for and how many were drawn ("Perf 10.0 s [Focused]: N frames asked, M submitted (P%); frame
# cycle A ms avg / B p95 ..."). The window read is the newest after half a minute, past the world's loading.
# This guards against a change that makes the frames slower; it does not stand for a real headset's rate, which is
# measured in one.
# World: Earth Planet (survival; the astronaut starts in the starter base, with its lights, screens and grids around).

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60
head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.25 1.0 -0.2
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.2
wait 35
remember submitted log '/Perf 10.0 s \[Focused\]: \d+ frames asked, \d+ submitted \((\d+)%\)/'
remember p95 log '/Perf 10.0 s \[Focused\]: .* frame cycle [\d.]+ ms avg / ([\d.]+) p95/'
# Nearly every frame the headset asked for was drawn, none of them very late.
expect number {submitted} >= 95
expect number {p95} <= 40
expect no log Exception
